# --- Development (recommended): dev server proxy → avoids browser CORS + OPTIONS preflight ---
# Copy to ".env.local" (gitignored). Restart `npm run dev` after changes.
#
# Backend base URL (ngrok, staging, etc.). Axios uses same-origin paths in dev;
# Quasar proxies these prefixes to API_PROXY_TARGET:
#   /client /catalogs /oauth /patients /staff /meet /telehealth /logout
# SockJS MUST go through the proxy in dev (telehealth-stomp uses relative /telehealth).
# Local API or ngrok tunnel. SockJS in DEV uses relative /telehealth → this proxy.
# Example ngrok: API_PROXY_TARGET=https://xxxx.ngrok-free.dev
API_PROXY_TARGET=https://your-api-host.example.com

# --- Optional: axios API base (REST). SockJS in DEV always uses relative /telehealth (proxy).
# Prefer leaving this unset in DEV when using ngrok — point API_PROXY_TARGET at the tunnel instead.
# If set to ngrok, axios works; SockJS still uses the proxy path in DEV (no browser CORS).
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://your-api-host.example.com

# --- GitHub Pages (production static hosting) ---
# There is no .env on the server: the SPA is pre-built. Configure the API URL as
# a repository variable so CI injects it during `npm run build`:
#   GitHub → repo → Settings → Secrets and variables → Actions → Variables
#   Name:  VITE_API_BASE_URL
#   Value: https://your-public-api.example.com   (no trailing slash)
# The deploy workflow passes it to the build step (see .github/workflows/deploy.yml).
# CORS must allow your Pages origin (e.g. https://<user>.github.io) on the API.

# Optional: Google Places (pharmacy address autocomplete). Prefer when set.
# VITE_GOOGLE_PLACES_API_KEY=

# Optional: Photon / OSM geocoder base URL (pharmacy search fallback).
# Dev defaults to /photon (Quasar proxies to https://photon.komoot.io).
# Prod defaults to https://photon.komoot.io — set a self-hosted URL for heavy use.
# VITE_PHOTON_BASE_URL=
